      "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nFixes #10929.\n\nUser text such as `Use {{idx}} literally` is currently changed to `Use 0 literally` during template encoding because `StringFormatter.apply` searches each previous replacement result. Inserted text can also consume a placeholder intended for the template itself.\n\nCollect each provided key's first occurrence from the original slot, then replace those ranges from right to left. This preserves literal content, the existing first-occurrence rule, unknown placeholders, type validation and special-token slots.\n\n### Validation\n\n- Added seven focused regression/control cases: the original implementation fails two and passes five; the fix passes the complete formatter module (57 tests).\n- A real offline `PreTrainedTokenizerFast` with the registered `empty` template confirms two training turns preserve `{{idx}}` after the fix.\n- Changed-file Ruff lint/format, applicable pre-commit hooks, actual commit hooks and full license check pass.\n- Whole-repository quality checks encounter existing EOF/format issues in `CLAUDE.md`, `template.py`, `tool_utils.py`, `patcher.py` and `supa_rms_norm.py`; their unrelated autofixes are excluded. The affected paths were clean before the checks.\n- An offline CPU attempt of the full suite with `--maxfail=1` stops at `test_feedback_data` because `llamafactory/tiny-random-Llama-3` is not cached. The focused formatter module and public encoding checks above pass.\n- Model training and GPU tests were not run; the complete repository suite did not pass locally.\n\nAI assistance was used for investigation, implementation and test review.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the [contributor guideline](https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?",
